   "bio": "Ajogu, born Ajogu Zekeri, is a Nigerian hip-hop and rap recording artist from Lagos State. Beginning his professional music journey in 2011 as Jay’ Major, he took a hiatus in 2018 before returning with a renewed identity and artistic direction as Ajogu.\n\nHis music blends reflective lyricism, faith, and contemporary hip-hop with Afro-influenced rhythms, exploring themes of process, pain, purpose, and emotional healing. Through his music, he tells deeply personal stories that connect with listeners on a human and spiritual level.\n\nHis body of work includes The Therapeutic Tape, featuring introspective records such as “Ọ́lẹlẹ (The Process Story)” and “Fela, Are You Proud of Me?”\n\nBeyond music, Ajogu leads the REVIVE Movement, a community-focused initiative creating spaces for live music, connection, and spiritual renewal through revival concerts across cities including Abuja.",
